{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\n`rebar-autodeploy-errors` changed state 6 times between 18:11 and 18:46 PDT on 2026-10-23 (01:11 to 01:46 UTC 2026-10-24): ALARM at 18:11, 18:26 and 18:41, OK at 18:16, 18:31 and 18:46 (CloudWatch `describe-alarm-history`). The alarm is `Sum` of `rebar/host:deploy_errors`, period 900s, 2 of 4 datapoints, `notBreaching`.\n\nThe raw metric (60s resolution, 17:04 to 18:59 PDT) holds exactly 2 non-zero datapoints, each Sum 1: 17:55 PDT and 18:00 PDT (00:55Z and 01:00Z). Every other datapoint is 0.\n\nHost journal, `rebar-autodeploy.service` (read-only SSM, instance i-00880b2c7f13527c5, host clock UTC): `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` reason `config_manual` at 00:53:31Z and 00:55:31Z, both naming target `10fd0737eb7`, plus an `AUTODEPLOY_DEFERRED` reason `review-in-flight` at 00:53:31Z for the same target.\n\nCommit `10fd0737eb7` (\"Condense reconciler and compose comments\") edits `infra/compose/gerrit.config`, which is in `CONFIG_PATHS` in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`. The non-comment, non-blank lines of that file are identical before and after the commit (checked by diffing the comment-stripped content of `10fd0737eb7~1` and `10fd0737eb7`). The commit message also says the configuration payload is preserved.\n\n## Root cause\n`autodeploy.sh` runs `changed \"$CONFIG_PATHS\"`, which is `git diff --name-only` between the deployed and target SHAs, and emits `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR config_manual` on any path difference. A comment-only or whitespace-only edit to a watched config file therefore reports a manual operator apply that does not exist. While a deploy is deferred (here `review-in-flight`), each timer tick re-runs the check and emits another error, which produced the 2 datapoints 5 minutes apart.\n\nThe repeated state changes are a separate effect of those 2 datapoints. CloudWatch re-aligns 15-minute buckets on each evaluation, so the 2 errors sit in adjacent buckets (2 of 4 breaching, ALARM) at some evaluations and in one bucket (1 of 4, OK) at others. ALARM fell on the :11/:26/:41 evaluations and OK on :16/:31/:46, which matches that alignment.\n\nNot established: whether the alarm's repeated state changes are intended behaviour for two close errors. The fix below addresses only the false error, not the alarm shape.\n\n## Approach\n1. In `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`, replace the bare path-difference test for `CONFIG_PATHS` with a helper that signals only when a changed config path differs in content after removing whole-line comments (first non-space character `#`, but not `#!`) and blank lines and trailing whitespace. Compare `git show <deployed>:<path>` with `git show <target>:<path>`.\n2. Fail toward signalling: a path added, removed, unreadable at either revision, or differing in any other line still emits `config_manual`. Comment syntaxes other than whole-line `#` (for example `;` in git-config files) are treated as content, so they still signal.\n3. Change nothing else in the autodeploy flow and do not change the alarm definition.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` and `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py`. Out of scope: the other detect-only classes (`nginx_edge_manual`, `nginx_materializer_manual`), the alarm period and datapoint settings, and the deferral logic.\n\n## Testing\nExtend the existing shell-stub test `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py`. Its git stub must answer `git show <sha>:<path>` with per-revision content so the new comparison has data. Cases:\n- a real content change to `infra/compose/gerrit.config` still emits `config_manual` (existing parametrized cases keep passing);\n- a comment-only change emits no `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`;\n- a whitespace-only change emits no `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`;\n- a change that mixes a comment edit with a content edit emits `config_manual`;\n- a path missing at one revision emits `config_manual`.\n```\npytest tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py -q\nmake verify\n```\nFailure case: before the change the comment-only test fails, because the script emits `config_manual` for it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `pytest tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py -q` passes, including a comment-only case that emits no `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` (checked: the test fails on main and passes after the change).\n- [ ] A content change and a mixed comment-plus-content change to a watched config path still emit `config_manual` (checked: parametrized tests).\n- [ ] `make verify` is green on the Linux CI gate (`Verified +1` on the Gerrit change).\n- [ ] After merge and deploy, the journal shows no `config_manual` for the next comment-only config commit (checked: `journalctl -u rebar-autodeploy` after such a commit, or recorded as not yet observed).\n","title":"A comment-only edit to a watched Gerrit config file emits AUTODEPLOY_ERROR config_manual and flaps rebar-autodeploy-errors"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792813907497993001,"uuid":"4be8a877-1b5c-4777-838f-ccf75d4c4250"}